    "sk2_size_guide": {
      "type": "sk2-size-guide",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "Find Your Perfect Fit",
        "subheading": "<p>Two measurements and one decision. That is all it takes to order the right kilt.</p>",
        "button_text": "View Size Guide"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "step_1": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Measure your waist",
            "text": "Wrap the tape where the kilt will sit — at the navel, higher than trousers — snug but not tight."
          }
        },
        "step_2": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Choose your length",
            "text": "Measure from that waistline to the top of your kneecap. Traditional kilts finish here; casual styles can sit slightly shorter."
          }
        },
        "step_3": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Select your style",
            "text": "Traditional, tartan, utility, leather, hybrid or contemporary. Each style page shows its own fit notes."
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "step_1",
        "step_2",
        "step_3"
      ]
    },
    "sk2_brand_story": {
      "type": "sk2-brand-story",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "Scottish Heritage. Modern Kilt Style.",
        "content": "<p>SCOTKILT exists for one reason: to make the kilt a piece you reach for, not a costume you rent.</p><p>We are a specialist. We do not sell tea towels, fridge magnets or postcards of castles. We sell kilts — and the tartans that make them — to customers on every continent who want the real silhouette, the right cloth and a fit that is properly explained.</p><p>Every tartan in the range is chosen for how it behaves in pleats, not just how it looks flat. Every style, from a full eight-yard traditional kilt to a black leather kilt, gets the same attention to waist, drop and hardware.</p><p>Heritage is the starting point. How you wear it is up to you.</p>"
      }
    },
