    "sk2_faq": {
      "type": "sk2-faq",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "Kilt & Tartan Questions",
        "subheading": "<p>Short answers to the questions we hear most.</p>"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "question_1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is a tartan kilt?",
            "answer": "<p>A tartan kilt is a pleated, wrap-around garment made from tartan cloth — a woven pattern of coloured stripes that cross at right angles to form a repeating check (the sett).</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I choose a tartan?",
            "answer": "<p>Start with family or clan associations if you have them, then think about colour. Universal tartans such as Black Watch suit anyone.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I measure for a kilt?",
            "answer": "<p>Measure your waist where you want the kilt to sit, then measure the drop to the top of your kneecap for length. Our size guide walks through each step.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is a utility kilt?",
            "answer": "<p>A utility kilt is a modern, casual kilt made from cotton canvas, usually with cargo pockets, belt loops and snap or buckle closures.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you ship internationally?",
            "answer": "<p>SCOTKILT is built as an international store. Delivery estimates and any duties are shown on our Shipping page and confirmed at checkout.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "question_1",
        "question_2",
        "question_3",
        "question_4",
        "question_5"
      ]
    },
    "sk2_seo_content": {
      "type": "sk2-seo-content",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "Premium Kilts & Scottish Tartans"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "paragraph_1": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Tartan kilts and Scottish kilts",
            "text": "<p>A tartan kilt is the original Scottish kilt: a length of woven cloth, pleated at the back and sides and flat across the front apron, fastened with leather straps and buckles. At SCOTKILT the tartan comes first.</p>"
          }
        },
        "paragraph_2": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Men's kilts for every occasion",
            "text": "<p>Traditional kilts are cut from a full length of cloth with deep knife pleats and a fringed apron edge — the silhouette for weddings, ceremonies and formal Highland dress. Casual-weight tartan kilts keep the same sett in a lighter build for everyday wear.</p>"
          }
        },
        "paragraph_3": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Utility, leather and hybrid kilts",
            "text": "<p>Utility kilts swap wool for cotton canvas, add cargo pockets and belt loops, and are made to be worn hard. Leather kilts bring structure and shine to the same silhouette. Hybrid kilts sit in between: tartan pleats with a plain canvas apron.</p>"
          }
        },
        "paragraph_4": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Choosing a Scottish tartan",
            "text": "<p>Universal tartans such as Black Watch can be worn by anyone. Clan tartans carry family associations. Our Tartan Finder sorts the range by colour and family so the choice is easier.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "paragraph_1",
        "paragraph_2",
        "paragraph_3",
        "paragraph_4"
      ]
    },
